10. Programs downloaded or installed on the user's machine
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These run as separate processes and are never linked into citegeist.

  GROBID, Apache-2.0, https://github.com/grobidOrg/grobid. Built from the release archive when
    the user installs it (pinned checksum), runs behind 127.0.0.1.
  Eclipse Temurin JRE 21, GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception, https://adoptium.net/. Downloaded
    for GROBID (pinned checksum). The Classpath Exception permits use by programs under any
    license.
  Pandoc, GPL-2.0-or-later, https://github.com/jgm/pandoc (source code and license).
    Downloaded from the upstream release when the user asks for text export (pinned checksum),
    or taken from the user's own installation. citegeist starts it as a separate process with
    command line arguments and files; it does not link to it and does not ship it.
  Claude Code, Codex CLI and Cursor CLI run as the user's own installations under the user's own
    accounts and terms. citegeist starts them through the Agent Client Protocol adapters
    @agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp and @agentclientprotocol/codex-acp (Apache-2.0).
  Zotero Connector: the user's browser extension, AGPL-3.0, talks to citegeist over the
    Connector protocol. citegeist contains no Zotero code. "Zotero" is a trademark of the
    Corporation for Digital Scholarship.

